{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A batch "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" dropped without delivering it, and why."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations14HTTPDropReportO","modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDropReport"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDropReport"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"HTTPDropReport.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport.swift#L16"},"title":"HTTPDropReport","roleHeading":"Enumeration"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Sending batches","anchor":"Sending-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"],"generated":true}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/SQ","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/SH","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDropReport","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Failure","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Error","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5ErrorP"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination reports every batch it drops for good on "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the endpoint rejected with a status that retrying won’t change, one whose request the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transport can never send, one whose request was still undelivered at its deadline, or one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its encoder couldn’t encode. It reports each record the encoder left out of a batch’s requests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"too. A batch whose send failed for a while and was then delivered isn’t reported, and neither"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is one whose delivery was cancelled. A dropped batch counts as received, so a store keeping its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records forgets them. A crash or a cancellation between a report and the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"acknowledgement leaves the store holding the batch, so after a relaunch the same record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identifiers can be reported again, as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/rejected(status:recordIDs:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","anch